        Thanks for the update. Model looks fine, but I have to admit I havent used min.sp before or GCV.Cp. Do these make a big difference? 

        About the difference between obs and model: perhaps remove the "id=1" part and see if that makes a difference? Its supposed to 
        force all smooths to have the same smoothing parameter, but perhaps we dont want the obs and the model to have the same sp. It 
        will be slower but Id be interested to see if it solves the large uncertainty issue.

        Not sure "fs" will make a difference. From memory, "sz"  was the new "fs", specifically designed to separate a main effect 
        from deviations, so I would stick with "sz".


